From eda315822f3b43465d8d44ba9056d351821fc189 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:38:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sid_exit: stop the label walking the workspace

All three repositioners (the per-frame pass, the click pass and the
IRQ_HANDLER branch in obj_c64_node Step_0) wrote sid_exit's Y
unconditionally, every frame, and none of them looked at what was already
parked at the destination. A node height recalculation or a dragged
MACRO_IRQ moved the label, and it regularly landed on another spine node.
Two connected nodes on one Y is the arrangement _walk_spine cannot
express - it takes the smallest Y strictly greater than the current one -
so the other node was silently dropped from the build.

scr_sid_exit_settle replaces all three bodies with one rule: the label is
only touched when it sits ABOVE where it has to be, and when it is moved,
anything occupying the slot is pushed clear first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019fUXqwJRpJfMBEpWBdeE1d
